    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (2/2 tests passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to expose `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`, on the owner API response.\n\nTwo edits, following the existing derived-field pattern (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema (a read-only string enum of `EMAIL`/`PHONE`). This is the OpenAPI spec that generates `OwnerDto` at build time, including the `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` type.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` backed by a `contactPreference(Owner)` helper that returns `EMAIL` when the email is present (non-null, non-blank) and `PHONE` otherwise.\n\nBecause both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` respond through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, the field is populated everywhere the owner is serialized. The two new tests \u2014 `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` \u2014 both pass, and no existing tests broke.",
